{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Analyzer",
  "description": "Analyzes modified source code files for potential improvements including code smells, design patterns, and best practices. Provides suggestions for improving readability, maintainability, and performance while preserving functionality.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "*.js",
      "*.css",
      "*.html",
      "*.json"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the code changes in the modified file for potential improvements. Focus on:\n\n1. **Code Smells**: Identify any code smells like long functions, duplicate code, complex conditionals, or unclear variable names\n2. **Design Patterns**: Suggest appropriate design patterns that could improve the code structure\n3. **Best Practices**: Check for JavaScript/CSS/HTML best practices including:\n   - Proper error handling\n   - Performance optimizations\n   - Accessibility improvements\n   - Security considerations\n   - Code organization and modularity\n4. **Readability**: Suggest improvements for code clarity and documentation\n5. **Maintainability**: Identify areas that could be refactored for easier future maintenance\n\nProvide specific, actionable suggestions while maintaining the existing functionality. Consider the project's vanilla JavaScript architecture and modular structure."
  }
}